 "labels": [
  {
   "language": "en",
   "status": "official",
   "text": "Section 55(d)(2)(B): the alternative minimum taxable income above which the unmarried-individual exemption phases out. Statutory $112,500 (2012 base); for taxable years beginning after 2017 section 55(d)(4)(A)(ii)(II) substitutes 50 percent of the dollar amount applicable under (2)(A). Years between the anchored rows are NOT pinned in this package (no Revenue Procedure text for them is in us.irc.inflation_adjustments): evaluation returns MISSING_PARAMETER_VALUE there instead of a fabricated indexed figure (TECH-GAPS, income-individual stage 2 AMT)."
  }
 ],
